{\b\fs28 dbx ZonePro 1260 Driver\par}
\par
{\b Overview\par}
This driver controls a dbx ZonePro 1260/1261 (and other ZonePro series) digital zone processor over RS-232 or TCP/IP. It implements the dbx open-loop protocol recommended for third-party controllers: commands are sent unacknowledged, and zone state (source, level, mute, scene) is tracked by the driver and exposed through system variables. State survives processor reboots via the driver's persistent store.\par
\par
{\b Connection\par}
RS-232: the ZonePro serial port is fixed at 57600 baud, 8 data bits, 1 stop bit, no parity, no handshaking. The driver automatically sends the required 1-second keep-alive ping and re-synchronizes the link when needed. The Device Online variable and the Connected/Disconnected events follow the ping replies from the unit.\par
TCP/IP: connect to the ZonePro's IP address on port 3804. The Device Online variable follows the TCP connection state.\par
\par
{\b Zone setup\par}
Each output zone is controlled through its Router (RTE) object inside the ZonePro configuration. The default object IDs in this driver match the ZonePro 1260 factory default configuration. If a custom configuration has been loaded with ZonePro Designer, look up each router's object ID by selecting it in the Program screen and pressing Ctrl+Shift+O (or capture a command with the Network Trace window, Ctrl+Shift+T) and enter the four hex bytes in the driver configuration. IMPORTANT: if the ZonePro configuration is changed, the object IDs may change too.\par
\par
{\b Levels\par}
The dbx protocol guide documents ZonePro faders as raw values 0..415 with 215 = 0 dB (10 counts per dB). Percent levels are scaled onto this range. If your configuration uses a different fader range, adjust the values in the Level Scaling category.\par
\par
{\b Scenes\par}
Recall Scene loads a stored scene in the unit. Because the driver is open loop, the unit does not report the parameter changes a scene causes, so zone variables may not reflect the device state until new commands are sent.\par
\par
{\b Custom commands\par}
The Send Custom Command function transmits any dbx message. Enter the bytes in hex starting at the Version byte (01). The driver adds the serial sync/framing/checksum automatically (or sends the message as-is over TCP).\par
\par
{\b Notes\par}
The controller uses node address 00 33 as documented by dbx for third-party controllers; do not set the ZonePro to that address. The ZonePro 1260 factory node address is 00 20.\par
}
